meet:
As I went walking up and down to take the evening air,
(Sweet to meet upon the street, why must I be so shy?)
I saw him lay his hand upon her torn black hair;

meets:
But thou wast deaf to the divine decree;
Young David meets thee, meets thee not in vain;
'Tis thine to perish on th' ensanguin'd plain.

meek:
That’s capable of worship, love, and loss;
We say the same of Shakspeare’s. I’ll be meek,
And learn to reverence, even this poor myself.

meed:
Is over; I have nothing left to fight;
Battles have always had their meed of music
But peace is quiet as a windless night.

meetin:
I 've journeyed 'roun' consid'able, a-seein' men an' things,
An' I 've learned a little of the sense that meetin' people brings;
